    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2DcBZNbSudGuxYj6Xtk3QZf)_\n\n## What\n\n`sp-litnotes-titles-dryrun` and `-convert` can now take the authors, year and title from the BibTeX entry of each note's citekey, so every litnote title can be brought to the `Last (Year) Title` standard.\n\n- `C-u M-x sp-litnotes-titles-dryrun`: BibTeX fills what the note lacks (`missing`).\n- `C-u C-u M-x sp-litnotes-titles-dryrun`: BibTeX wins over the meta lines (`always`).\n- `sp-litnotes-titles-bibtex` sets the mode without a prefix argument (default nil, so nothing changes unless asked).\n- The dry run still writes nothing. The report shows the proposed titles, marks values taken from BibTeX (`from BibTeX: authors, year`), and lists notes whose citekey has no entry. `convert` is unchanged otherwise (one confirmation, backups).\n\n## How\n\n- Reuses `sp-litnotes-meta--field`/`--year` (braces, LaTeX accents to Unicode, year from `date` or `crossref`) and `sp-author-notes-bibtex--files`.\n- New `sp-litnotes-meta-build-index`: the `.bib` files are read once per run (in a first background slice) into `sp-litnotes-meta--index`; `sp-litnotes-meta--entry` uses it when set. Without it, behaviour is as before.\n- Source edited in `sp-org-lint.org` and `sp-litnotes-meta.org` and tangled. Five new ERT tests; `sp-litnotes-titles` and `sp-litnotes-meta` tests all pass on Emacs 29.3 (20/20). Not run on the real vault.\n\n## Ambiguities I resolved\n\n- `sp-bibtex-dir` no longer exists (merged into `sp-bibliography-dir`), so the files come from the usual registered list.\n- Names come from the `author` field only, never `editor`. `and others` is dropped, a name wholly in braces is one name, and last names are used as written (so no accent-insensitive matching is needed for titles).\n- In `missing` mode an ambiguous `pub-author` also counts as lacking.\n- Citekeys must match the entry exactly; the first key with an entry wins.\n- Values typed in during `convert` win over BibTeX. Meta lines are not written; `sp-litnotes-meta-fill` does that.\n- No CHANGELOG edit (nightly tidy). Branch is the session's designated `claude/project-thread-g1foaj`, not a number-prefixed name, since the number was unknown before opening.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9Nriy9znKJgpzJLJU)_",
